.TH EUCLID-CLI-EDS-CREATE-ZONE 1 "November 2026" "euclid-cli 2.3.2" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eds-create-zone \- create a zone the name server answers for
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eds create-zone
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I ZONE
[\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
[\fB\-\-description\fR|\fB\-d\fR \fITEXT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a zone. From then on the name server answers for every name in
it: with the records put into it, and with NXDOMAIN for every other
name. A new zone holds only its SOA and NS records.
.PP
The name is lowercased and a trailing dot is dropped, so
.I Corp.Example.
and
.I corp.example
are the same zone.
.PP
.B The name is unique across the installation,
not only within your account \- a DNS question names no account, so
there can be only one zone of a name to answer it from. A name another
account already has is refused as existing, the same as one of your
own.
.PP
A zone inside another is allowed, and wins for the names below it:
with both
.I corp.example
and
.I lab.corp.example
stored, a question about
.I host.lab.corp.example
is answered from the second.
.PP
The zone belongs to your account and to the namespace your session is
scoped to, which is what its ERN is built from.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fIZONE\fR
The zone's apex, e.g.
.IR corp.example .
Required. Cannot contain a wildcard, and cannot be in
.IR euclid.internal ,
which holds the names euclid gives what it runs.
.TP
.BR \-\-ttl " " \fISECONDS\fR
TTL of every record in the zone that does not set its own, and how long
a resolver may cache an answer saying a name or a type is not there.
Defaults to 300.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-description " " \fITEXT\fR
Free text, shown by
.BR euclid-cli-eds-get-zone (1)
and
.BR euclid-cli-eds-list-zones (1).
.SH OUTPUT
The zone, as JSON:
.IR name ,
.IR ern ,
.IR namespace ,
.IR ttl ,
.IR description ,
.IR recordCount ,
.IR serial ,
.I created
and
.IR modified .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The zone was created.
.TP
.B 1
A zone of that name exists already (HTTP 409), the name is not a valid
domain name or is in
.IR euclid.internal ,
the TTL is negative or larger than 2147483647, or a grant does not allow
it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eds create-zone --name corp.example
euclid-cli eds create-zone --name lab.corp.example --ttl 30 \e
    --description "test machines, changed often"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eds (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-put-record (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-delete-zone (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-change-namespace (1)
